.TH LT-QWWAD_DENSITY_OF_STATES "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_density_of_states (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_density_of_states \- compute density of states in 1D, 2D and 3D systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_density_of_states
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find density of states for bulk (3D), quantum wells (2D) and quantum wires (1D).
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.HP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-mass\fR ] arg (=0.067) Effective mass (relative to free electron).
.TP
\fB\-\-vcb\fR arg (=0)
Band\-edge potential [eV]
.TP
\fB\-\-alpha\fR arg (=0)
Non\-parabolicity parameter [eV^{\-1}]
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e) ID of particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or 'l', for
electrons, heavy holes or light holes
respectively.
.TP
\fB\-\-ndim\fR arg (=2)
Dimensionality of the system (1, 2 or 3)
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'E*.r'   Energies of subband minima (only needed for 2D or 1D systems):
            Column 1: state index.
            Column 2: energy [meV].

.SS Output files:
   'rho.r'  Density of states:
            Column 1: energy [meV]
            Column 2: d.o.s. [J^{-1}m^{-n}]
            Note that the unit for d.o.s. depends on the number of dimensions 'n'.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the density of electron states in a bulk system with effective mass = 0.1m0:
    qwwad_density_of_states --mass 0.1 --ndim 3

Compute the density of heavy-hole states in a 2D system with mass = 0.62 m0 and non-parabolicity = 10 eV^{-1}:
    qwwad_density_of_states --mass 0.62 --alpha 10 --ndim 2
